{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"carried_from":"prior finding 1","checklist_item":"- [ ] Decide and document how rebar.bridge_fsck() / the MCP tool surface an operational RebarError (catch and re-shape, or update the contract docstring), since only the CLI currently maps it to exit 2.","criteria":["error-handling","regression","api-compat"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["src/rebar/_lib_ops.py:87: `findings = audit_bridge_mappings(Path(tracker))` with no try/except","_unknown_event_types_from_ref raises via `_scan_error` -> `RebarError(message, returncode=2, stderr=message)` (bridge_fsck.py:83-85, 138-140)","CLI main() catches it: `except RebarError as exc: ... return 2` (bridge_fsck.py:619-623 region)","Library docstring still asserts 'A nonzero exit (anomalies present) is NORMAL, not an error' (_lib_ops.py:77) and does not mention the new raising path","MCP tool: `return BridgeFsckOut.model_validate(rebar.bridge_fsck())` (_mcp_reads.py:272) — a raised RebarError becomes a tool error rather than a returned result"],"finding":"rebar.bridge_fsck() (library) and the MCP bridge_fsck tool call audit_bridge_mappings directly and do not catch RebarError, so an operational git scan failure now raises an uncaught exception through the library/MCP surfaces, whereas previously bridge_fsck() never raised. Only the CLI main() translates RebarError to exit 2.","id":"0","impact":0.3,"location":"src/rebar/_lib_ops.py:87","norm_id":"n0b95912ca2c0f333","priority":0.3,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed